WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.680
Look directly down from above, just as we finish reversing parallel to the curb.

00:05.360 --> 00:11.460
As the car reverses around center X, the wheels at E and F travel along the two dashed circles.

00:11.980 --> 00:16.220
Meanwhile, the front right corner A of our car sweeps along the outer circle.

00:16.700 --> 00:18.860
In the tightest possible parking space,

00:19.100 --> 00:23.340
that corner A will just barely miss the corner G of the car parked in front.

00:23.980 --> 00:28.040
Because corner A passes right through point G along that outer circle,

00:28.040 --> 00:32.540
both A and G lie at the exact same distance from the center X.

